      "id": "p1",
      "description": "Both words end in one vowel + one consonant (refer, offer).",
      "marks": 1
     },
     {
      "id": "p2",
      "description": "In re-FER the stress is on the last syllable, so the r is doubled.",
      "marks": 1
     },
     {
      "id": "p3",
      "description": "In OF-fer the stress is on the first syllable, so the r is not doubled.",
      "marks": 1
     }
    ]
   },
   "markingNotes": "Example answer: Both end in a single vowel and consonant. The rule is to double before a vowel suffix only when the stress is on the last syllable: refer is stressed on -fer, so referred; offer is stressed on of-, so offered."
